# Experiment 5 - Prompt Optimization

## Basic Prompt

```text
Tell me about Artificial Intelligence.
```

## Basic Output

Artificial Intelligence (AI) is a technology that allows computers to perform tasks that usually require human intelligence.

### Improved Prompt

```text
Write a 150-word explanation of Artificial Intelligence for BS Computer Science students. Include its definition, applications, advantages, challenges, and future scope in simple English.
```

## Improved Output

Artificial Intelligence (AI) is a branch of computer science that enables machines to perform tasks such as learning, problem-solving, and decision-making. AI is used in many fields, including healthcare, education, banking, transportation, and cybersecurity. It helps automate repetitive tasks, improves accuracy, and saves time. Although AI offers many benefits, it also creates challenges such as privacy concerns, ethical issues, and job displacement. As technology continues to grow, AI is expected to become an important part of everyday life and create new opportunities for innovation. Learning AI is valuable for Computer Science students because it is one of the fastest-growing fields in technology.

## Observations

The improved prompt produced a longer, more organized, and more useful response. It covered all the requested points and was easier to understand than the basic prompt.

## Improvements

Adding a specific writing style, word limit, or target audience can make the response even more accurate and relevant.

---

# Conclusion

These experiments showed that writing better prompts leads to better AI responses. Different prompt engineering techniques help improve the quality, accuracy, and clarity of AI-generated content. By using Role Prompting, Chain-of-Thought Prompting, Few-Shot Prompting, Structured Output, and Prompt Optimization, it becomes easier to get responses that match the required task. Learning prompt engineering is an important skill for anyone working with modern AI tools.

